{"reference":"Proverbs 23","book":"Proverbs","chapter":23,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Justice and Material Life","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Verses 10–11 warn against moving an old boundary marker to take land from the fatherless. This belongs to a broader Proverbs concern: it can relate material outcomes to diligence and choices, yet it also directly condemns gaining advantage through exploitation or the denial of justice.","verse_refs":["Proverbs 23:10-11"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_proverbs_023_fc10d709a01cff31ea9dc895"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"A Wider Wisdom Collection","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Proverbs 22:17–24:22 has unusually close sequences of themes and expressions with the Egyptian Instruction of Amenemope. This observation concerns the larger collection that includes Proverbs 23, rather than a direct claim about any one verse in this chapter.","verse_refs":["Proverbs 22:17-29","Proverbs 24:1-22"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_proverbs_023_28708aa2b07867a1590ed978"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}